WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.900
From 1994, cheap Dyclofenac cut India's vultures to 1,000th and added over 100,000 deaths yearly. This is unintended consequences episode 151. A pain killer meant for working cattle, a scavenger collapsed, nobody measured, a sanitation gap that reached people, a band that leaked, and the test that was never required. Dyclofenac began as a human drug. In the 1970s, it was developed as a non-steroidal anti-inflammatory for arthritis.

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:31.880
this, and for pain after surgery.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:34.740
It did what that class of drugs is built to do.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:38.300
It eases swelling, it gave people back ordinary movement.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:44.640
When the patent lapsed in the early 1990s, Indian pharmaceutical firms made inexpensive versions.

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:46.860
Farmers could finally afford a dose.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:52.140
Before that shift, livestock owners had few practical options for the pain and inflammation

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:55.280
that cut milk yields and draft power in working animals.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:01:01.380
a bullock that could not plow was not only an animal in distress, it was a season of fieldwork at

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:06.920
risk. The drug therefore looked like a straightforward welfare gain and a productivity gain for millions

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:12.980
of smallholders who had watched cattle suffer without treatment. No one at the time tested the compound

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:18.500
on the obligate scavengers that cleaned the countryside of dead livestock. That omission was not

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:24.400
a secret plot. It was a blank in the file. In the absence of any published data on avian kidney

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:30.220
physiology, the decision carried no visible downside for the people who made the drug or administered it.

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:36.340
Farmers in the Gangetic Plane and in Rajasthan, where cattle densities were highest, saw immediate

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:42.200
improvements in animal mobility after a single low-cost injection. The same dose that ease joint

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:47.100
swelling in a bullock also kept the animal productive for another season of plowing or hauling.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:53.020
Because Dyclofenac was already approved for human use, regulators treated the extension to livestock

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:57.240
stock as a minor administrative step, rather than a new environmental release.

00:01:57.860 --> 00:01:59.940
The economic logic was simple arithmetic.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:04.860
One vile treated several animals at a fraction of the price of imported alternatives.

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:09.040
Milk output or fieldwork could resume within days instead of weeks.

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:14.400
For a small holder counting days until the next milking or the next planting, that arithmetic

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.780
was hard to argue with.

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:17.780
The intended patient was the cow.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.320
The intended return was work and milk.

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:24.040
Both of those showed up quickly, and both of those were easy to see.

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:29.220
By the mid-1990s, veterinary use had spread rapidly through the cattle belt of Northern

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:30.360
and Western India.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:35.640
Roadside pharmacies and livestock markets stocked the human formulation and vials labeled

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:36.240
for cattle.

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:40.440
Farmers injected animals shortly before slaughter or natural death.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:45.960
Early surveys by the Bombay Natural History Society recorded no obvious change in carcass

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:46.440
availability.

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:50.500
Vultures still arrived in large numbers at known feeding sites.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:55.260
If you were standing at one of those sites in those years, the old picture still held.

00:02:55.820 --> 00:03:01.640
Birds came, carcasses went, a few ornithologists noted occasional dead birds with white urate

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:02.900
deposits around the vent.

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:07.800
Those incidents were treated as isolated disease events rather than a systemic threat.

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:11.180
That reading was available from the evidence then in hand.

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:16.280
A handful of dead birds, against flocks that still filled the sky, did not yet look

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:21.540
like a collapse. The scale of adoption can be traced in pharmacy sales records. Once

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:26.160
the molecule entered the generic market, annual production volumes rose from laboratory

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:31.420
quantities to hundreds of tons. That was enough to dose millions of cattle each year across

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:36.380
states where open grazing was the norm. Because the human and veterinary supply chains were

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:41.700
not yet separated by regulation, the same blister packs moved from urban hospitals to rural

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:46.640
veterinary shops with minimal friction. A drug approved for people did not have to change

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:52.380
plants or packaging logic, or much of its root to reach a bullock. Early monitoring focused

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:57.720
on whether the drug reduced clinical signs in livestock, no parallel program tracked residue

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:03.180
levels in the carcasses those livestock left behind. The first systematic knee crops that

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:08.400
later linked the drug to vulture mortality were still years away, so the absence of reported

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:13.660
problems was taken as evidence of safety. Silence in the data was read as a clean result.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:19.700
It was, more precisely, a result no one had yet gone looking for. The causal chain began when

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:25.140
a treated animal died and its carcass retained enough dichlofenac residue to kill any vulture that

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:30.040
fed on it. The bird did not have to receive an injection. It only had to do the work it had

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:36.400
always done. In 2004, Jay Lindsay Oaks and colleagues published in Nature the experimental proof.

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:41.700
Oral doses matching those found in treated livestock produced the visceral gout and kidney

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:44.040
failure already seen in field carcasses.

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:48.980
The white deposits ornithologist had noted years earlier were not a scattered disease.

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:51.080
They were a signature of the drug.

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:57.460
By 2007, the Oriental Whitebacked Vulture had declined to one-tenth of 1% of its early

00:04:57.460 --> 00:05:03.080
1990s numbers, according to repeated road transect surveys reported in PLOS-1.

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:10.820
A 97% drop recorded between the early 1990s and 2007 left two few birds to process the

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:14.220
daily volume of livestock mortality across the subcontinent.

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:19.680
Three gyps species that had once numbered in the tens of millions were, within a decade

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:21.540
of the generic flood, a remnant.

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:26.200
The arithmetic of exposure is straightforward once the residue data are examined.

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:30.620
A single treated buffalo could contain several lethal doses for a vulture.

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:33.340
Jip species feed in groups of dozens.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:38.240
One contaminated carcass could remove multiple breeding adults in a single afternoon.

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:41.860
Without those adults returning to nests, recruitment collapsed.

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:47.240
The loss was not only of birds in the air, it was of the next generation that those birds

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:47.900
would have raised.

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:53.120
With the primary scavengers gone, the carcasses that once disappeared within hours lay

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:56.140
rotting for days at village dumps and urban waste sites.

00:05:56.140 --> 00:06:00.340
rates. That persistence was the first visible rearrangement of the countryside.

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:06.300
Feral dog populations rose sharply because an abundant previously contested food source

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:12.160
was now uncontested. Each additional dog raised the probability of a human bite. India

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:17.220
already accounted for roughly a third of global rabies deaths, so the bite risk landed on

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:21.940
a country that was already carrying a heavy share of that disease. At the same time,

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:26.880
Some uneaten carcasses leached pathogens into shallow aquifers and streams used for washing

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:27.560
and irrigation.

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:31.860
Surface water near carcass dumps showed elevated bacterial loads.

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:36.740
The effect concentrated in the same districts that had once supported the dense's vulture

00:06:36.740 --> 00:06:37.180
colonies.

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:41.300
The sanitation gap therefore ran through two measurable pathways.

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:46.000
More dogs and dirtier water in the places where the birds had been thickest.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:51.780
Economists A.L. Frank and Anant Sudarshan used the natural experiment of districts that

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:54.440
historically differed in vulture habitat suitability.

00:06:54.800 --> 00:07:01.500
In the American Economic Review, they estimated that all cause human mortality rose 4.7% in

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:04.940
high suitability districts between 2000 and 2005.

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:10.320
Districts that had supported the largest vulture populations recorded human death rates more

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:14.600
than 4% higher than comparable districts that had never hosted many vultures.

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:14.720
measures.

00:07:15.380 --> 00:07:21.560
The 4.7% increase reflects both direct zoonotic risk and the broader degradation of local

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:24.480
water quality once the keystone scavenger was removed.

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:30.440
A narrow approval for a cattle pain killer had, through residue, kidney failure, and an

00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:33.000
emptied sky, become a public health number.

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:39.140
India banned veterinary dikelofenac in 2006 and strengthened the prohibition in 2008.

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:44.980
The response was real, it was also late relative to the collapse already measured, and it had

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:47.300
to work through supply chains that had already mixed.

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:53.480
Follow-up Carcass surveys published in PLOS-1 showed the prevalence of DicloFenac contaminated

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:59.900
livestock fell from roughly 10.8% before the ban to 6.5% several years later.

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:03.700
That fall slowed the declines, it did not stop them.

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:10.520
Necropsees of vultures found dead between 2008 and 2012, reported in Oryx, revealed that

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:12.500
some birds still carried diklofenac.

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:17.180
Others showed nemisolide residues associated with the same gout ethylogy.

00:08:17.820 --> 00:08:21.980
Human formulation diklofenac continues to be diverted into veterinary channels.

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:28.060
Populations of the three-gip species remain at a few percent of pre-1990s levels, with

00:08:28.060 --> 00:08:29.620
only modest signs of recovery.

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:34.540
The persistence of the drug after the formal ban illustrates the difficulty of separating

00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:39.720
two parallel supply chains that share the same molecule and the same manufacturing plants.

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:46.040
Even after the 2008 tightening, which required colored dyes and larger vial sizes for human

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:50.180
formulations, enforcement relied on state level pharmacy inspections.

00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:53.780
Those inspections could not monitor every rural transaction.

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:56.360
A dye and a bigger vial are signals.

00:08:56.360 --> 00:09:02.980
cells. They are not a seal on every roadside shop. Meanwhile, alternative non-steroidal anti-inflammatory

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:08.220
drugs such as Nymisulide entered the veterinary market without the same level of pre-release

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:13.220
testing against vulture kidney tissue. The original oversight was reproduced at a smaller

00:09:13.220 --> 00:09:18.740
scale. The band changed the label. It did not, by itself, change the question regulators

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:25.360
had failed to ask in 1994. When regulators approved Dyclofenac for livestock, they evaluated

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:29.800
it only the intended patient species and the immediate economic return to farmers.

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:34.240
The process rewarded any low-cost drug that cleared livestock quickly.

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:39.020
It did not require tests on the scavengers whose removal would later impose sanitation

00:09:39.020 --> 00:09:40.540
costs in human lives.

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:43.360
A second principle sits beside that one.

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:49.500
Once a compound enters widespread agricultural use, a later ban on the veterinary formulation

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:53.980
can still be undermined by leakage from the parallel human supply chain that regulators

00:09:53.980 --> 00:09:59.460
continue to authorize. The burden that was missing is a demonstration of safety for the entire

00:09:59.460 --> 00:10:04.860
local scavenger community before marketing approval. That requirement would move the proof from

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:10.220
post-release mortality counts to pre-release feeding trials. If you follow how an ecological

00:10:10.220 --> 00:10:16.100
loss shows up inside human death rates, environmental intelligence on the Narrow Network stays with

00:10:16.100 --> 00:10:21.520
that kind of measurement. The same narrow gate still opens whenever a livestock medicine is cleared

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:23.580
on how fast a herd returns to work.

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:29.260
If a new anti-inflammatory or antibiotic is approved for cattle on productivity data alone,

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:31.320
what would you look for in the file?

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:36.280
A feeding trial on the animals that eat the dead, or only a note that the cow stood

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:36.800
up sooner?

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:38.580
That's the case for today.

